        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "summary",
            "heading": "Key ideas from this article",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "\"I don't want engineering or medicine\" is not one reason."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "That timeline needs to be priced in honestly, not discovered halfway through."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:2",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Product Roles: the Highest Realistic Ceiling",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "This is the strongest option on this entire list if your excluded reason was disliking the JEE grind rather than disliking logical or technical work itself."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Most of these accept any 12th stream with around 50% aggregate and no JEE-style entrance exam."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Skipping Class 12 Maths does not mean skipping algorithmic thinking, probability, or basic statistics."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "tech",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 2
          },
          {
            "needId": "detail:6",
            "type": "detail",
            "heading": "Four Questions Before You Commit",
            "kind": "items",
            "items": [
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "The four questions keeps this decision grounded in your actual situation instead of which track sounds most respectable once engineering and medicine are gone."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Ask what kind of daily work you actually want: building and debugging, numbers and models, design and portfolio work, arguing a case, lab research without patients, or structured exam-driven public service."
              },
              {
                "heading": "",
                "text": "Ruling out engineering because you disliked pure maths and physics is a different signal than ruling it out because you disliked the exam grind."
              }
            ],
            "sourceSectionId": "checkpoint",
            "sourceNeedIndex": 6
          }
        ]
      },
      "type": "summary",
      "title": "Reason Before You Pick a Replacement Track"
